      "environment_kind": "definition",
      "source_line_start": 407,
      "source_line_end": 418,
      "current_tex": "\\begin{definition}[Bounded Set]\n\\label{def:bounded}\nLet $A\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}$. The set $A$ is \\emph{bounded} if it is bounded\nabove and bounded below; equivalently,\n\\[\n  (\\exists \\ell,u\\in\\mathbb{R})(\\forall a\\in A)(\\ell\\leq a\\leq u).\n\\]\nEquivalently, $A$ is bounded if\n\\[\n  (\\exists M\\geq 0)(\\forall a\\in A)(|a|\\leq M).\n\\]\n\\end{definition}",
      "formalizations": []
    }
  },
  "creation_mode": "prompt"
